        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Xoşkîn',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Xoşkîn is a Kurdish trick-taking card game similar to 3-player double-deck Pinochle. Played in eastern/southeastern Turkey (Northern Kurdistan). Features bidding and melds. Also known as Nezere or Pinîkêr. Name possibly derived from English 'Auction' via 'Okşin'.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "This Kurdish trick-taking game with bidding is played in the eastern and south-eastern parts of Turkey, unofficially known as northern Kurdistan. Xoşkîn is almost identical to the American game of three-handed double deck Pinochle; the alternative name Pinîkêr reflects that. As Levent Suberk suggested, the name Xoşkîn likely derives from the English 'Auction', probably via 'Okşin'. A version played by Turkish workers in Düsseldorf has been documented by Thomas Beil.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
